To be a success in this role you’ll need to be proficient in design practices such as wireframing, usability testing and prototyping. You’ll also need to be confident in front of people and working with others as this role is client facing. In particular, we imagine that you
Are an Experienced UX Designer
Can drive and manage projects;
Can gather the threads and produce reports based on your findings;
Can deliver client workshops;
Are proficient in wireframing tools such as Figma;
Can create storyboards, user flows, process flows and site maps;
Can work alongside designers and developers to bring ideas to life;
Are able to undertake UX Research tasks from usability testing to stakeholder interviews;
Have advanced proficiency in both Danish and English.

Translate strategy and insights into well considered journeys, wireframes and visual interface designs rooted in robust design principles;
Presenting your work to clients and stakeholders, handling input and managing feedback;
Collaborate with global DEPT® colleagues to help international clients reach their digital goals;
Foster a design-driven culture through knowledge sharing and best practices

4+ years of experience as UX/UI designer at an agency or renowned brand;
